# Population census spike (Phase 22, D-07): start in an anarchy system and dump the
# ship census. Needs the throwaway probe OXP (not in the repository), passed with
#   run-remote.sh --steps tools/oolite-reference/steps/census-anarchy.steps \
#     --addons /home/opencode/oolite-probes/population-census --out DIR --timeout 300
# The probe's scenarios.plist adds two scenarios after the four built-ins (standard,
# easy, tutorial, strict). Loading a scenario populates the system, and the probe's
# world script logs one CENSUS-SHIP line per ship, then CENSUS-DONE.
# Menu arithmetic: the runner holds every key for 0.5 s, and Oolite repeats a held
# arrow key about every 0.2 s, so ONE press moves the selection TWO rows (measured:
# four Down presses landed on the second row in two runs). The selectable rows are
# Return to Menu, Normal, Easy, Tutorial, Strict, Census anarchy, Census quiet (seven,
# wrapping, starting on Normal), so two Down presses select "Census anarchy (Qudira)".
# The probe logs the system name, so a wrong landing shows in Latest.log.
window 120
sleep 10
shot title
key Return
sleep 3
shot scenarios
sleep 2
key Down
sleep 4
key Down
sleep 4
shot scenario-selected
key Return
waitlog 180 CENSUS-DONE
sleep 3
shot docked
